   "also": "xw_o/xe_o are planned from the spo source (x_o column x 786, y 1777) up to the N edge (y 2073.6), along it, and down the W/E edge to y 1390-1690: ~1.5x the direct horizontal length, and the stations sit on the outline edge; spo r_q/x_q -> u_ist_xw_o_0 up to 444 um. x_o last station -> S out pin 397 um + next spine N input reg 12 um = 409 > 405 (hd_spn)"
  },
  {
   "id": "C2",
   "what": "Reset leaf: the RTL default rst_n (bound to tap relay u_rrl_27 = rst_n_t9, site 518.4,864 = outline centre) still drives every non-FIRM leaf (u_spo/u_spr control flops at x~940 y 1770-2065) and the internal-station epoch flops (u_ist_*/eq). reset_taps.tcl re-points only face/ft FIRM flops (26+22 / 25+20). Leaf hops up to 2035 um (28 / 25 sinks), violating the reset rule (decision 2, every hop <= 405 um); recovery path ~2 mm on one relay."
  },
  {
   "id": "C3",
   "what": "Clock load: sinks concentrate in the x 750-1260 band; nearest-tap load clk_t22 3938 / 2810, clk_t23 2353 / 2354, clk_t2 2393 (hd_spn) while 8 W-half taps carry 2-8 sinks (reset relays only). Guidance (WARN), not a gate, but the 1500 cap reassignment (<= 200 um) cannot absorb it; zero/near-zero taps need the hd_turn condition (prune or declare unloaded for tap balance)."
  },
  {
   "id": "C4",
   "what": "Sign-off basis not yet in the kits: constraint.sdc has one vclk with source latency 250 for both corners (no shared per-corner FF vclk, decision 9.7/5e), and the flow sources plain platforms/asap7/setRC.tcl (no F2 RCX-calibrated SET_RC_TCL / rc_fit)."
